":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2024-06-25T00:50:51Z","updated_at":"2024-06-28T10:52:44Z","closed_at":"2024-06-28T10:52:13Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.2.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows10 all renderers\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhile the window mode is Fullscreen under any of the 3 StretchModes and any Renderer if the base resolution of the viewport is changed the viewport will snap to the top left (bottom left when using opengl) instead of remaining in the center and will scale in a weird way:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/assets/69814029/c5fd563d-39bc-44d9-a635-9a873fba4177\r\n\r\nas can be seen the viewport doesn't remain centered instead snapping to the corner. this can be solved by toggling fullscreen off then on again but it is annoying when having a resolution setting in some menu in your game.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n(see minimal reproduction project)\r\n\r\ngo into fullscreen and then change the viewport base resolution through code.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[viewport_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/15962756/viewport_bug.zip)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"DissonantVoid","id":69814029,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5ODE0MDI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69814029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dissonant